{{wikipedia|dab=riddle (disambiguation)|mul=Riddle}}
==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|ɪdəl}}

===Etymology 1===
{{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|redel|lang=enm}}, {{term|redels|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{term|rædels|rǣdels|lang=ang}}, {{term|rædelse|rǣdelse|lang=ang|counsel", "opinion", "imagination", "riddle}}, from {{proto|Germanic|rēdislijan|counsel, conjecture|lang=}}. Akin to {{etyl|osx|-}} ''[[radisli|rādisli]]'' ({{etyl|nl|-}} ''[[raadsel]]''), {{etyl|goh|-}} ''[[radisle|rādisle]]'' ({{etyl|de|-}} ''[[Rätsel]]'' "riddle"), {{etyl|ang|-}} ''[[rædan|rǣdan]]'' "to read, advise, interpret"

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A [[verbal]] [[puzzle]], [[mystery]], or other [[problem]] of an [[intellectual]] nature, such as "It's black, and white, and red all over. What is it?"

=====Synonyms=====
* [[enigma]], [[conundrum]], [[brain-teaser]]

=====Derived terms=====
* [[riddler]]
* [[riddle stick]]
* [[a riddle wrapped up in an enigma]]

